WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.330
London, on the River Thames,
had 8.80 million people in 2021.

2
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:15.130
In 2024, it had the highest GDP per
person of any UK region: 72,201 pounds.

3
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.390
That is 2.4 times the North East's.

4
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:23.910
In the G a WC ranking, London is one of
only two Alpha plus plus world cities,

5
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.730
with New York.

6
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.370
So why can so many
Londoners not afford a home?

7
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.590
Are London wages simply low?

8
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.230
In this mission, you'll
trace how migration,

9
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.390
from the rest of the UK and from abroad,
shaped London's growth and character.

10
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.390
Then you'll test which statistics
reveal who struggles in a rich city.

11
00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.710
Your mission: explain why so many
Londoners cannot afford a home,

12
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.830
despite London's high output.
